       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg add little blood pressure benefit and raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia.\n\nCould you check whether this is a typo or a deliberate dose? Here are some options:\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO daily** is the max standard dose. If the patient is currently on 5 mg, this would be the usual titration step.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO daily** is the usual starting dose. Some patients start at 2.5 mg.\n- **Add a second agent**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, if 10 mg isn't controlling BP. This is generally preferred over going above the max.\n\nIf you do want 20 mg, please confirm with your supervising resident or attending and tell me. I can enter it with a note recording that the dose was verified. If you'd rather change the dose, tell me which one and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
